                            "value": "How many persons sit between T and V?",
                            "comp": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eDirections: \u003c/strong\u003eRead the following information carefully and answer the question that follows.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eSeven persons \u0026ndash; E, H, K, P, T, V, and Z \u0026ndash; are sitting around a circular table facing the centre not necessarily in the same order. Each person likes a different colour \u0026ndash; Red, Blue, Green, Yellow, Pink, Orange, and White not necessarily in the same order.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eThe one who likes Red sits second to the right of K. E sits immediately between the persons who like Pink and Yellow. K neither likes Pink or Yellow nor sit adjacent to them. The person who likes Yellow sits second to the left of the one who likes Orange. H sits immediate left of the person who likes White. The person who likes White is not an immediate neighbour of the one who likes Red. Only one person sits between V and the one who likes Orange (either clockwise or anticlockwise). Z sits third to the left of the person who likes Blue. T is not an immediate neighbour of the person who likes Orange.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n",
